Trota Fleet agent
=================

Connects this device to a Trota Fleet panel, where it appears with its
status (system, uptime, memory, disk, addresses, pending updates, kiosk
page) and from where it can receive a few commands:

  - show another page on the kiosk, restart the kiosk browser;
  - install the available updates;
  - reboot.

The device calls the panel over HTTPS once a minute: no port is opened on
the device. The panel cannot run any other command or program.

Enrolment (the code is created in the panel, Dispositivi → Aggiungi):

  sudo trota-fleet-agent enroll https://fleet.example.com <code>
  sudo systemctl enable --now trota-fleet-agent

With cloud-init, for many devices at once:

  #cloud-config
  write_files:
    - path: /etc/trota-fleet.conf
      content: |
        TROTA_FLEET_URL=https://fleet.example.com
        TROTA_FLEET_TOKEN=<code>

Other commands: trota-fleet-agent status (the report sent to the panel),
trota-fleet-agent once, trota-fleet-agent leave.
Files: /etc/trota-fleet.conf, /var/lib/trota-fleet/device.json (root only).
